Overlay patch 0046: sky stereo sentinels (= reference 0033 concept, MK64
chokepoint; VISION-PRO-LUS-PLAYBOOK §2.6).
MK64's sky is STRUCTURALLY unlike OoT's: Sky::Draw renders ortho gradient
quads (guOrtho loaded G_MTX_PROJECTION), DrawSkyActors renders yaw-mapped
screen-space cloud/star/snow sprites under the shared HUD ortho, and
Sky::DrawFloor the below-horizon gradient. Zero-disparity ortho puts the
sky ON the panel — stereoscopically in FRONT of distant terrain. 0044's
injector applies a constant per-eye horizontal NDC shift to ortho passes
BETWEEN these sentinels (the background-disparity term, sky-at-infinity);
all other ortho (HUD/menus, which share the same ortho machinery — the
sentinels are the ONLY way to tell them apart) stays on the panel plane.
Single chokepoint: CM_RaceDrawSky covers Draw + DrawSkyActors + DrawFloor
for every caller (race screens + ending sites). The thunderbolt fill-box
is drawn by the callers AFTER this function — correctly outside.
Microcode note: this port compiles F3DEX_GBI=1, so game-side G_NOOP is
0xc0 (not F3DEX2's 0x00); the interpreter routes it to the same noop
handler whose p-byte convention 0044 hooks (0x5A begin / 0x5B end).
Emitted via gDisplayListHead (this game's DL cursor). __IOS__-guarded.
REV3 (VR R15 item 5): a third pair — 0x60/0x61 around DrawFloor, the
below-horizon ground fill, so the rear-view pane can drop it.
REV2 (VR R13 item 4): a second, finer pair — 0x5E/0x5F around DrawSkyActors
— so 0044 can tell the yaw-KEYED sprites from the yaw-INDEPENDENT gradient
and floor. The rear-view pane keeps the latter and drops the former.

--- a/src/port/Game.cpp
+++ b/src/port/Game.cpp
@@ -563,11 +563,70 @@
 void CM_RaceDrawSky(ScreenContext* screen, s32 someId) {
     // if (bDrawSkybox) {
     if (CVarGetInteger("gDrawSky", true) == true) {
+#ifdef __IOS__
+        // SOH_IOS (overlay 0046): stereo sky sentinel BEGIN — 0044 shifts
+        // ortho passes between these to place the sky at infinity.
+        {
+            Gfx* sohTag = gDisplayListHead++;
+            sohTag->words.w0 = (uintptr_t)((G_NOOP << 24) | (0x5A << 16));
+            sohTag->words.w1 = 0;
+        }
+#endif
         Sky::Instance->Draw(screen);
+#ifdef __IOS__
+        // SOH_IOS (overlay 0046 rev2, VR R13 item 4): SPRITE-SPAN sentinels.
+        // Everything between 0x5A and 0x5B is "the sky", but it is two
+        // structurally different things: Sky::Draw's gradient quads and
+        // DrawFloor's below-horizon quad are SCREEN SPACE and yaw-independent,
+        // while DrawSkyActors' cloud/star texrects are keyed to the camera's
+        // yaw (and re-keyed to the composed eye by 0051). The rear-view pane
+        // needs the first and must not have the second, and R11's shift of the
+        // whole ortho pass moved both — which is why the pane has had no sky.
+        {
+            Gfx* sohTag = gDisplayListHead++;
+            sohTag->words.w0 = (uintptr_t)((G_NOOP << 24) | (0x5E << 16));
+            sohTag->words.w1 = 0;
+        }
+#endif
         if (gGamestate != CREDITS_SEQUENCE) {
             func_80057FC4(screen, someId); // DrawSkyActors
         }
+#ifdef __IOS__
+        {
+            Gfx* sohTag = gDisplayListHead++;
+            sohTag->words.w0 = (uintptr_t)((G_NOOP << 24) | (0x5F << 16));
+            sohTag->words.w1 = 0;
+        }
+#endif
+#ifdef __IOS__
+        // SOH_IOS (overlay 0046 rev3, VR R15 item 5): the GROUND-FILL span.
+        // Sky::DrawFloor paints vtx[4..7] — the BELOW-HORIZON half of the sky,
+        // a full-width screen-space colour ramp from the course's FloorTop down
+        // to FloorBottom — on every course except Rainbow Road. In the eyes it
+        // is harmless (the ground covers it). In the REAR-VIEW PANE it is the
+        // only thing that can produce the user's "grey empty space where the
+        // uphill road behind should be", so 0044 needs to be able to tell it
+        // apart from the sky gradient above the horizon.
+        {
+            Gfx* sohTag = gDisplayListHead++;
+            sohTag->words.w0 = (uintptr_t)((G_NOOP << 24) | (0x60 << 16));
+            sohTag->words.w1 = 0;
+        }
+#endif
         Sky::Instance->DrawFloor(screen);
+#ifdef __IOS__
+        {
+            Gfx* sohTag = gDisplayListHead++;
+            sohTag->words.w0 = (uintptr_t)((G_NOOP << 24) | (0x61 << 16));
+            sohTag->words.w1 = 0;
+        }
+        // SOH_IOS (overlay 0046): stereo sky sentinel END.
+        {
+            Gfx* sohTag = gDisplayListHead++;
+            sohTag->words.w0 = (uintptr_t)((G_NOOP << 24) | (0x5B << 16));
+            sohTag->words.w1 = 0;
+        }
+#endif
     }
 }
 
